      }
    ],
    "budget": "Before create, the existing typed runtime validator validates the selected complete VM envelope, subtracts512MiB and500m CPU from its client allowance, and verifies actual Linux caller memory.max/cpu.max/no-swap. Under mac16 and the explicitly selected existing lifecycle override, caller0.5CPU/3GiB plus one helper0.5CPU/512MiB consumes1CPU/3.5GiB inside the1CPU/4GiB slot. This arithmetic is admission capacity, not measured simultaneous node/Pod/client fit.",
    "helper_controls": "Factory uses --pull=never, immutable digest, explicit platform, root0:0, exact /bin/sh -c command-v, finite0.5CPU/512MiB, MemorySwap equal Memory,64PIDs, no network, private cgroup namespace/default private PID namespace, read-only root, no added capabilities/dropALL, no-new-privileges, restartno and one64MiB tmpfs. Parsed actual observations independently reject missing/null/changed caps, host PID/network/cgroup modes, ownership/source/name/image/command substitutions, mounts beyond its tmpfs, unsafe restart/isolation and non-created/nonzero-PID/already-started states.",
    "seriality": "Docker atomic creation of the fixed name derived from a stable caller owner coordinate permits at most one extant helper for that coordinate. A competing same-coordinate proof fails create instead of spending the same reservation twice. This is exclusion, not a queue and not global admission for multiple clients; the outer operator must still run one heavy/qualification role at a time and enforce aggregate active client/helper inventory.",
    "identity": "The code validates the returned canonical Docker CID, inspects and starts that exact CID, and checks expected deterministic name, immutable target, owner/source labels and command twice: after create and after copied executable/source verification immediately before start. The original immutable executable and copied source-byte comparison remains. Owner environment and labels are binding coordinates, not authentication by themselves; the concrete guardian must join them to the selected actual caller and helper CID. Historical656 source cannot satisfy a future225 image-source comparison merely by being labeled225.",
    "cleanup": "The created valid CID enters existing owned-scenario cleanup before copy/start; normal and exception paths remove that exact CID and retain cleanup failures. Name exclusion is released only by actual removal. An asynchronous interruption in the narrow create-to-cleanup-registration interval can leave a never-started container/name; it does not authorize reuse, broad removal or an invented clean state. Concrete supervision still needs exact inventory/retirement, including a running helper if the caller is forcibly terminated.",
    "limitations": "This refiner authenticates neither its observation producer nor future concurrent Docker mutations. Future supervision must pin the actual selected Docker context, stable caller owner/CID, cached current image, caps and enrolled identities; no implicit VM startup/image build or permissive inventory whitelist is admitted."
  },
